{"id":"4c40d683c32409463631803728a01c5855fdc972","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"4c40d683c32409463631803728a01c5855fdc972","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/serving/online_serving/derenderer.md","lines":["@@ -124,6 +124,8 @@ The server keeps no state between calls. Everything the next call needs is in `s"," "," `/inference/v1/generate` returns `GenerateLogProbs` with integer `token_id`s (the generate server has no tokenizer), and derender turns those into `ChatCompletionLogProbs` / `CompletionLogProbs`, filling `token` and `bytes` from the tokenizer with the usual U+FFFD byte-fallback correction. Generate returns every top-k candidate the engine produced; derender keeps the ones the coupled endpoint would, with the same helpers: the first `top_logprobs` on chat (all of them for `top_logprobs=-1`) and the first `logprobs + 1` on completions (all of them for `logprobs=-1`). It reads those values from `chat_request` / `completion_request`, so without the original request, or with one that does not ask for logprobs, it returns every candidate. Requests that use `logprob_token_ids` get no output logprobs from generate (their `sampling_params.logprobs` is unset), so derender has none to return for them either. Streaming derender does the same per chunk on both the plain detokenization path and the parser path (see [Streaming state and logprobs](#streaming-state-and-logprobs)). As on `/v1/chat/completions`, a request with `include_reasoning: false` and a parser configured gets no logprobs at all, batch or streaming, since the decoded logprob tokens would reveal the hidden reasoning."," ","+For both chat and completion derender, `return_tokens_as_token_ids` in `chat_request` / `completion_request` takes precedence over the answering render server's `--return-tokens-as-token-ids`. `true` returns `token_id:N` logprob tokens (`bytes: null` in the chat shape); explicit `false` returns decoded strings even when the server flag is enabled. An omitted or `null` value, or no original request, uses the render server's flag. This applies to full responses and streaming chunks, including top logprobs. It does not change decoded message content or completion text, or the suppression of logprobs when reasoning is hidden.","+"," ## Streaming cost"," "," Streaming derender threads a client carried `stream_state` across per-chunk calls instead of keeping session state on the server."],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/serving/online_serving/token_in_token_out.md","lines":["@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ print(response[\"choices\"][0][\"token_ids\"])"," "," ### Derender"," ","-`derender` returns the assistant `message` a coupled `/v1/chat/completions` would, without a separate [derender](derenderer.md) call. `/v1/chat/completions/render` and `/v1/messages/render` return `parse_context` on the `GenerateRequest`. Send it back with `output_mode: \"derender\"`. It carries the tools, `tool_choice`, `include_reasoning`, resolved JSON only `chat_template_kwargs` and the history tool call count. A `parse_context` field this server doesn't know fails a `derender` request and is ignored at the other levels.","+`derender` returns the assistant `message` a coupled `/v1/chat/completions` would, without a separate [derender](derenderer.md) call. `/v1/chat/completions/render` and `/v1/messages/render` return `parse_context` on the `GenerateRequest`. Send it back with `output_mode: \"derender\"`. It carries the tools, `tool_choice`, `include_reasoning`, `return_tokens_as_token_ids`, resolved JSON only `chat_template_kwargs` and the history tool call count. A `parse_context` field this server doesn't know fails a `derender` request and is ignored at the other levels."," "," - The parser reads the engine's `text`, so it sees the stop string cut and the post `adjust_request` decode flags. That makes it match coupled chat for parsers whose `adjust_request` changes decoding which `/derender` can't."," - A server with a tool or reasoning parser needs `parse_context`. Without a parser, `message.content` is the plain text.","@@ -108,6 +108,10 @@ data: {\"request_id\": \"...\", \"output_mode\": \"derender\", \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0,"," "," With `output_mode: \"tokens\"`, logprobs are `GenerateLogProbs` with an integer `token_id` and `rank` per entry and no `token` or `bytes` (see [Generate Output Logprobs](renderer.md#generate-output-logprobs)). With `output_mode: \"text\"`, they are `ChatCompletionLogProbs` carrying the decoded token strings and their UTF-8 `bytes` for the sampled token and every entry in `top_logprobs`; a server started with `--return-tokens-as-token-ids` returns `token_id:N` placeholders there instead, as `/v1/completions` does."," ","+With `output_mode: \"derender\"`, `parse_context.return_tokens_as_token_ids` overrides the generate server's `--return-tokens-as-token-ids` when it is not `null`: `true` returns `token_id:N` placeholders with `bytes: null`, and `false` returns decoded tokens and UTF-8 bytes even when the server flag is enabled. An omitted or `null` value uses the generate server's flag. `/render` preserves explicit `true` and `false` without applying the render server's flag, and omits the context field when the request value is omitted or `null`. This setting affects logprobs only; the assistant message is still parsed from text.","+","+Upgrade generate nodes before using explicit request overrides: older generate nodes reject `parse_context.return_tokens_as_token_ids` with a 400 in derender mode. Requests with an omitted or `null` override remain compatible because `/render` leaves that field out. Unknown parse-context fields remain ignored in `tokens` and `text` modes.","+"," ### Errors"," "," The server returns a 400 for:"],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/derender/test_derender.py","lines":["@@ -25,8 +25,9 @@"," "," "," @pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")","-def server():","-    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(MODEL_NAME, []) as remote_server:","+def server(request):","+    args = getattr(request, \"param\", [])","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(MODEL_NAME, args) as remote_server:","         yield remote_server"," "," ","@@ -1970,3 +1971,54 @@ async def test_derender_completion_preserves_requested_token_ids(","         )","     assert choices[0].token_ids == (token_ids if return_token_ids else None)","     assert choices[0].prompt_token_ids == (prompt_ids if return_token_ids else None)","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"server\", \"server_flag\"),","+    [([], False), ([\"--return-tokens-as-token-ids\"], True)],","+    indirect=[\"server\"],","+    scope=\"module\",","+)","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"endpoint\", [\"chat\", \"completion\"])","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"override\", [None, False, True])","+async def test_derender_logprob_override(","+    client, tokenizer, server_flag, endpoint, override","+):","+    \"\"\"An explicit false must override a true render-server default.\"\"\"","+    token_id = tokenizer.convert_tokens_to_ids(\"▁true\")","+    logprobs = _make_generate_logprobs(token_id)","+    logprobs[\"content\"][0][\"top_logprobs\"][0][\"token_id\"] = token_id","+    generated = _make_generate_response(","+        [token_id], finish_reason=\"length\", logprobs=logprobs","+    )","+    original = (","+        {\"messages\": [], \"logprobs\": True, \"top_logprobs\": 1}","+        if endpoint == \"chat\"","+        else {\"prompt\": \"Hi\", \"logprobs\": 1}","+    )","+    if override is not None:","+        original[\"return_tokens_as_token_ids\"] = override","+    payload = (","+        {\"chat_request\": original, \"generate_response\": generated}","+        if endpoint == \"chat\"","+        else {\"completion_request\": original, \"generate_responses\": [generated]}","+    )","+    response = await client.post(","+        f\"/v1/{'chat/completions' if endpoint == 'chat' else 'completions'}/derender\",","+        json=payload,","+    )","+    response.raise_for_status()","+    placeholders = server_flag if override is None else override","+    expected = f\"token_id:{token_id}\" if placeholders else \" true\"","+    choice = response.json()[\"choices\"][0]","+    if endpoint == \"chat\":","+        entry = choice[\"logprobs\"][\"content\"][0]","+        assert (entry[\"token\"], entry[\"bytes\"]) == (","+            expected,","+            None if placeholders else list(b\" true\"),","+        )","+        assert entry[\"top_logprobs\"][0][\"token\"] == expected","+    else:","+        assert choice[\"logprobs\"][\"tokens\"] == [expected]","+        assert choice[\"logprobs\"][\"top_logprobs\"] == [{expected: -2.0}]"],"additions":54,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/derender/test_derender_stream.py","lines":["@@ -2263,8 +2263,9 @@ async def test_too_many_choices_rejected(self):"," "," "," @pytest.fixture(scope=\"module\")","-def server():","-    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(MODEL_NAME, []) as remote_server:","+def server(request):","+    args = getattr(request, \"param\", [])","+    with RemoteLaunchRenderServer(MODEL_NAME, args) as remote_server:","         yield remote_server"," "," ","@@ -2833,3 +2834,66 @@ async def test_stream_parsed_missing_prompt_token_ids_rejected(parser_client):","     )","     assert resp.status_code == 400","     assert \"prompt_token_ids\" in resp.json()[\"error\"][\"message\"]","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"endpoint\", \"server\", \"server_flag\"),","+    [","+        (endpoint, args, flag)","+        for endpoint in (\"chat\", \"parsed\", \"completion\")","+        for flag in (False, True)","+        for args in [","+            ([\"--return-tokens-as-token-ids\"] if flag else [])","+            + (","+                [\"--tool-call-parser\", \"hermes\", \"--enable-auto-tool-choice\"]","+                if endpoint == \"parsed\"","+                else []","+            )","+        ]","+    ],","+    indirect=[\"server\"],","+    scope=\"module\",","+)","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"override\", [None, False, True])","+async def test_streaming_derender_logprob_override(","+    client, tokenizer, server_flag, endpoint, override","+):","+    \"\"\"Plain/parsed chat and completion chunks honor the request override.\"\"\"","+    token_id = tokenizer.convert_tokens_to_ids(\"▁true\")","+    logprobs = _generate_logprobs([token_id])","+    logprobs[\"content\"][0][\"top_logprobs\"] = [{\"token_id\": token_id, \"logprob\": -0.5}]","+    chunk = _make_stream_chunk(","+        [token_id], finish_reason=\"length\", logprobs=logprobs","+    ).model_dump(mode=\"json\")","+    chat = endpoint != \"completion\"","+    original = (","+        {\"messages\": [], \"logprobs\": True, \"top_logprobs\": 1}","+        if chat","+        else {\"prompt\": \"Hi\", \"logprobs\": 1}","+    )","+    if override is not None:","+        original[\"return_tokens_as_token_ids\"] = override","+    response = await client.post(","+        f\"/v1/{'chat/completions' if chat else 'completions'}/derender\",","+        json={","+            \"stream\": True,","+            \"prompt_token_ids\": tokenizer.encode(\"Hi\"),","+            \"generate_chunk\": chunk,","+            \"chat_request\" if chat else \"completion_request\": original,","+        },","+    )","+    response.raise_for_status()","+    placeholders = server_flag if override is None else override","+    expected = f\"token_id:{token_id}\" if placeholders else \" true\"","+    choice = response.json()[\"chunk\"][\"choices\"][0]","+    if chat:","+        entry = choice[\"logprobs\"][\"content\"][0]","+        assert (entry[\"token\"], entry[\"bytes\"]) == (","+            expected,","+            None if placeholders else list(b\" true\"),","+        )","+        assert entry[\"top_logprobs\"][0][\"token\"] == expected","+    else:","+        assert choice[\"logprobs\"][\"tokens\"] == [expected]","+        assert choice[\"logprobs\"][\"top_logprobs\"] == [{expected: -0.5}]"],"additions":66,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/derender/test_generate_logprobs_conversion.py","lines":["@@ -170,3 +170,25 @@ def test_unknown_top_id_does_not_shift_the_other_candidates():","         (\"\", None),","         (\"ok\", list(b\"ok\")),","     ]","+","+","+def test_token_id_placeholders_preserve_sampled_and_top_logprobs():","+    logprobs = GenerateLogProbs(","+        content=[","+            GenerateLogProbsContent(","+                token_id=SECOND_BYTE,","+                logprob=-0.5,","+                top_logprobs=[","+                    GenerateLogProb(token_id=FIRST_BYTE, logprob=-1.5),","+                ],","+            )","+        ]","+    )","+    resolved = _resolve_logprobs(","+        logprobs, _StubTokenizer(), return_tokens_as_token_ids=True","+    )","+    entry = resolved.content[0]","+    assert (entry.token, entry.bytes, entry.logprob) == (\"token_id:11\", None, -0.5)","+    assert [(top.token, top.bytes, top.logprob) for top in entry.top_logprobs] == [","+        (\"token_id:10\", None, -1.5)","+    ]"],"additions":22,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/render/test_render.py","lines":["@@ -1184,3 +1184,19 @@ async def test_messages_render_tool_search_result_for_deepseek_v41(","         \"<｜User｜><tool_result>get_weather</tool_result>\\n\\n\"","         \"<tool_result>notes</tool_result><｜Assistant｜>\"","     ) in detokenize.json()[\"prompt\"]","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"override\", [\"omitted\", None, False, True])","+async def test_render_omits_null_token_id_override(client, override):","+    \"\"\"Default requests must not send a new field to older generate nodes.\"\"\"","+    body = {\"model\": MODEL_NAME, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hi\"}]}","+    if override != \"omitted\":","+        body[\"return_tokens_as_token_ids\"] = override","+    response = await client.post(\"/v1/chat/completions/render\", json=body)","+    response.raise_for_status()","+    context = response.json()[\"parse_context\"]","+    if override is None or override == \"omitted\":","+        assert \"return_tokens_as_token_ids\" not in context","+    else:","+        assert context[\"return_tokens_as_token_ids\"] is override"],"additions":16,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_generate_stream.py","lines":["@@ -1590,10 +1590,10 @@ def set_history_tool_call_count(self, count):","         self.history_tool_call_cnt = count"," "," ","-def _derender_serving(engine, parser_cls=_StubParser):","+def _derender_serving(engine, parser_cls=_StubParser, **kwargs):","     \"\"\"Serving whose derenderer builds real stream processors around","     `parser_cls`, or plain ones when it is None.\"\"\"","-    serving = _build_serving_tokens(engine)","+    serving = _build_serving_tokens(engine, **kwargs)","     derenderer = serving.online_derenderer","     derenderer.parser = parser_cls","     derenderer.enable_auto_tools = False","@@ -1878,3 +1878,46 @@ async def mock_generate(*args, **kwargs):","         .delta.content","         == \"a\"","     )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"server_flag\", [False, True])","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"override\", [None, False, True])","+async def test_stream_derender_logprob_request_override(server_flag, override):","+    engine = _mock_engine()","+","+    async def mock_generate(*args, **kwargs):","+        yield _make_request_output(","+            \"req-1\",","+            token_ids=[10],","+            text=\"é\",","+            finish_reason=\"length\",","+            finished=True,","+            logprobs=[","+                {","+                    10: Logprob(logprob=-0.5, decoded_token=\"é\"),","+                    11: Logprob(logprob=-1.5, decoded_token=\"e\"),","+                }","+            ],","+        )","+","+    engine.generate = MagicMock(side_effect=mock_generate)","+    serving = _derender_serving(engine, return_tokens_as_token_ids=server_flag)","+    request = _derender_request(ParseContext(return_tokens_as_token_ids=override))","+    request.sampling_params.logprobs = 2","+    parsed = await _collect_sse(await serving.serve_tokens(request))","+","+    chunk = parsed[0]","+    assert chunk[\"output_mode\"] == \"derender\"","+    choice = chunk[\"choices\"][0]","+    assert choice[\"delta\"][\"content\"] == \"é\"","+    entry = choice[\"logprobs\"][\"content\"][0]","+    placeholders = server_flag if override is None else override","+    assert (entry[\"token\"], entry[\"bytes\"]) == (","+        (\"token_id:10\", None) if placeholders else (\"é\", [195, 169])","+    )","+    assert [(top[\"token\"], top[\"bytes\"]) for top in entry[\"top_logprobs\"]] == (","+        [(\"token_id:10\", None), (\"token_id:11\", None)]","+        if placeholders","+        else [(\"é\", [195, 169]), (\"e\", [101])]","+    )"],"additions":45,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/entrypoints/scale_out/token_in_token_out/test_serving_tokens.py","lines":["@@ -923,3 +923,73 @@ async def test_abort_requests_is_served_without_tokens_only(client):","         \"/abort_requests\", json={\"request_ids\": [\"generate-tokens-unknown\"]}","     )","     assert resp.status_code == 404","+","+","+@pytest.mark.asyncio","+@pytest.mark.skipif(","+    envs.VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND,","+    reason=\"The Rust frontend does not support /render\",","+)","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(","+    (\"server\", \"server_flag\"),","+    [","+        ([\"--gpu-memory-utilization\", \"0.3\"], False),","+        ([\"--gpu-memory-utilization\", \"0.3\", \"--return-tokens-as-token-ids\"], True),","+    ],","+    indirect=[\"server\"],","+    scope=\"module\",","+)","+async def test_derender_logprob_request_override(client, server_flag):","+    \"\"\"Both derender routes must use the same tri-state override as coupled chat.\"\"\"","+    for override in (None, False, True):","+        request = {","+            \"model\": MODEL_NAME,","+            \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hi\"}],","+            \"max_completion_tokens\": 2,","+            \"temperature\": 0,","+            \"logprobs\": True,","+            \"top_logprobs\": 2,","+        }","+        if override is not None:","+            request[\"return_tokens_as_token_ids\"] = override","+        coupled = await client.post(\"/v1/chat/completions\", json=request)","+        assert coupled.status_code == 200, coupled.text","+        expected = coupled.json()[\"choices\"][0][\"logprobs\"]","+        assert expected and expected[\"content\"]","+        placeholders = server_flag if override is None else override","+        if placeholders:","+            # Both derender paths keep generate text mode's null bytes","+            # for placeholders; coupled chat currently includes bytes.","+            # Normalize only that existing representation difference.","+            for entry in expected[\"content\"]:","+                entry[\"bytes\"] = None","+                for top in entry[\"top_logprobs\"]:","+                    top[\"bytes\"] = None","+        # Separate requests can differ slightly in floating-point logprobs.","+        # Keep token strings, bytes and the remaining structure exact.","+        for entry in expected[\"content\"]:","+            entry[\"logprob\"] = pytest.approx(entry[\"logprob\"], abs=1e-3)","+            for top in entry[\"top_logprobs\"]:","+                top[\"logprob\"] = pytest.approx(top[\"logprob\"], abs=1e-3)","+        rendered = await client.post(\"/v1/chat/completions/render\", json=request)","+        assert rendered.status_code == 200, rendered.text","+        payload = rendered.json()","+        for mode in (\"derender\", \"tokens\"):","+            generated = await client.post(","+                \"/inference/v1/generate\", json={**payload, \"output_mode\": mode}","+            )","+            assert generated.status_code == 200, generated.text","+            result = generated.json()","+            if mode == \"tokens\":","+                derendered = await client.post(","+                    \"/v1/chat/completions/derender\",","+                    json={","+                        \"model\": MODEL_NAME,","+                        \"chat_request\": request,","+                        \"prompt_token_ids\": payload[\"token_ids\"],","+                        \"generate_response\": result,","+                    },","+                )","+                assert derendered.status_code == 200, derendered.text","+                result = derendered.json()","+            assert result[\"choices\"][0][\"logprobs\"] == expected"],"additions":70,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/entrypoints/launchers/api_server/app_state.py","lines":["@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@ async def init_app_state(","         default_chat_template_kwargs=default_chat_template_kwargs,","         reasoning_effort_map=args.reasoning_effort_map,","         log_error_stack=args.log_error_stack,","+        return_tokens_as_token_ids=args.return_tokens_as_token_ids,","     )"," ","     state.serving_tokenization = ServingTokenization("],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/entrypoints/launchers/render/app_state.py","lines":["@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ async def init_render_app_state(","         default_chat_template_kwargs=default_chat_template_kwargs,","         reasoning_effort_map=args.reasoning_effort_map,","         log_error_stack=args.log_error_stack,","+        return_tokens_as_token_ids=args.return_tokens_as_token_ids,","     )"," ","     state.openai_serving_models = model_registry"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/entrypoints/scale_out/render/serving.py","lines":["@@ -233,6 +233,7 @@ def _build_parse_context(","             tool_choice=request.tool_choice,","             parallel_tool_